  "notes": {
    "architecture": "Covers full backboardd touch forwarding pipeline from path collection through IOHIDEventSystemConnectionDispatchEvent.",
    "drop_condition_stealing": "bb_system_gesture_stealing_gate checks [x8, #0x31] (systemGestureIsStealingEvents). If non-zero, event is released without dispatch.",
    "drop_condition_no_connection": "bb_forward_task_conn_gate checks x20 (connection from clientForTaskPort). If NULL, event drops to bb_forward_task_drop (0x1000135d8).",
    "drop_condition_cfmachport": "bb_client_for_task_cfport checks CFMachPortCreateWithPort. If port is dead or invalid in backboardd, returns NULL.",
    "drop_condition_destinations": "bb_destinations_gate checks unique client count w24. If 0 (CA hit test / taskPortOfContextId yielded no ports), drops to 0x1000169bc -> exit.",
    "caps": "Use --max-hits bb_=0 --max-hits ui_=0 --max-hits hid_client_=0 --max-hits ca_=0 for unlimited coverage of touch routing events.",
    "touch_owner_architecture": "Hooks CA server context creation (0x1842ff72c / 0x1842ff7c4) and local context creation (0x1842f7760) to log all context IDs, client task ports, and client PIDs. Dumps CA::Render::Context (x1:256) at ca_context_task_result (0x184389738) to reveal context_id (+0xc), client PID (+0x90), task port (+0x98), client port (+0x9c), and root layer pointer (+0xb0). Tracks backboardd boot progress overlay (PUIProgressWindow at level 2999.0) creation and dismissal."
  }
